    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the areas of the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the slant height of the pyramid:**\n   The slant height is the height of one of the triangular faces. It can be found using the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the slant height, the height of the pyramid, and half the side length of the base.\n   The height of the pyramid is 12 cm, and half the side length of the base is 5 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Slant height} = \\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 144} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total area of the four triangular faces:**\n   There are four triangular faces, so the total area of the four triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total surface area of the pyramid:**\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the total area of the four triangular faces.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
